# L §4.3: a def's written `at e` sets its law date (tally 1's rule that a time key sets it is gone), and L §5.11 step
# 2: a rule with v V "exists only where V governs", among "the versions of one rule that exist at d and K".  g[2015]
# is read at gifts_from[2015] = 2015-07-01, where gv governs: 5.00 USD.  (The reads inside e are made at the reader's
# law date; gifts_from governs always.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2014-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

unit USD: currency minor 0.01
source s "s"
index yr = year 2014..2016
input gifts_from[y in yr]: date
input amt: money USD
def g[y in yr]: money USD at gifts_from[y]
  rule base v gv = amt

version gv
  cite s
  governs 2015-07-01..
  known 2014-01-01

version facts
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2014-01-01
  gifts_from[2015] = 2015-07-01
  amt = 5 USD

ask q: g[2015]
=== expect
q: 5.00 USD
  cut 2026-12-31
